        ":question/id": "c7ab1fc4-f7f2-55b9-a74c-b824a475ac09",
        ":question/problem": "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{3t},\\,y=2{e}^{t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$  \n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{\u2032}(t)}{{x}^{\u2032}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=3{e}^{3t},\\,{y}^{\u2032}(t)=2{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{3{e}^{3t}}=\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-2t}.\n$$",
